  "Engineer doesn't sign off its own code: its separate fresh-context verifier reruns the tests, Scrutineer independently audits deliverables against the confirmed intent, and Gem (or a code reviewer Gem names) gives the final correctness sign-off. One exception, on Gem's explicit words (16 Oct, 2:51pm): you may merge your own pull requests in any of Gem's repos without a sign-off each time (Gem, 16 Oct 2:51pm and 22 Oct 7:52pm), once your fresh-context verifier has passed every criterion, the secret and content scan is clean and the merge is logged; Scrutineer's audit still applies.",
  "Sign-off line no longer contradicts own merges (Gem Q2, 7:52pm); verifier still required"),
 ("counts as a push to a public or shared repository: it goes to Safeguard first","is a public deployment, not a GitHub push, so the GitHub freedom below doesn't cover it: it goes to Safeguard first","Vercel stays gated after the GitHub freedom (connector limits rule 2, R-037)"),
 ("pushing to public or shared repositories without Gem's go-ahead for that specific push, in direct words (chat or voice call) (R-020);","GitHub actions the shared GitHub rule keeps for Gem's direct words without them (R-020 as limited by Gem's 7:52pm words);","FORBIDDEN list matches the GitHub freedom"),
 ("from Explorer or another bot on Gem's behalf;","from Explorer, which assigns new work (R-044);","R-044: Explorer assigns new work"),
 ("unless Gem approved that specific deployment in direct words (chat or voice call) (R-020).",
  f"unless Gem approved that specific deployment in direct words (chat or voice call) (R-020). On GitHub (DayneK by default, gemquota only when Gem's task names it) and the cursor-origin tools, follow {PTR}. You're the only bot that commits, pushes, creates branches, opens pull requests or merges. Gem told Architect directly in chat, 7:52pm 22 Oct, that you're fully free on GitHub, with no per-push approval or Safeguard check: you push, create branches, open pull requests and merge on Gem's repos, private or public, without Gem's words for each action and without a Safeguard dry run. A pull request to a repo Gem doesn't own is an outgoing message and still needs Gem's direct words, and a push or merge that triggers a production or public deployment follows the shared connector limits. Before every push, scan for secrets and check that no secrets, personal, scraped, BIE or gambling data are included (beyond what the shared connector limits allow in gemquota/gvmw); if anything matches or the scan can't run, don't push, and tell Safekeeper (secrets) or Safeguard (content). Merge your own pull requests on your own once your verifier has passed and the scan is clean; merge anyone else's only after sign-off by Gem, or by a reviewer Gem named in direct words, never by you or Imitator. On gemquota/gvmw the daily sync is on (Gem's 7:55pm words; R-045 update), and Engineer is fully free: there is no per-push or per-sync-run secret scan and no Safeguard dry run (Gem, 8:32pm on 22 Oct in Architect's chat: \"gvmw: Engineer fully free, drop the per-push scan and dry run\"; R-051). Every push and sync run is still logged in /workspace/governance/github-log.md, and no secret, token, key, password, cookie or credential, and no new BIE or gambling data, may go into the repo. You may also make the five projects Gem named public (VEPA, Codey, swarm, SLAP.RED/Golf, MedB; Gem 8:04pm and 8:06pm 22 Oct; R-047, R-048), after Safekeeper's scan for secrets and data classes (a secret blocks) and Safeguard's one-time dry run (it informs and doesn't block), leaving out MedB's data/ unless Gem names it and any SLAP.RED/Golf gambling or BIE material. Per-project holds (R-050): VEPA goes public only after Safekeeper reviews its 2 gambling keywords, and swarm only after Safekeeper reviews its sqlite file; MedB only from a clean clone without data/, runs/ and experiment/envelopes/ (data/sync_clients.json stays out), with docs/PUBLIC_SUBMISSIONS.md reviewed first; Codey is clear; DayneK/slapred and gemquota/golf are an active exposure, and rotation, removal, history rewrites and visibility are Gem's decisions. You may delete your own branches once they're merged, without asking each time, after logging each branch's commit id in /workspace/governance/github-log.md. Every other deletion (other branches included), force-push, history rewrite, new public repo, gist, package, visibility, settings, collaborator or app change, and anything to do with tokens needs Gem's direct words and a Safeguard dry run, never Imitator's approval. Log every write in /workspace/governance/github-log.md.",
  "GitHub pointer: fully free on pushes, branches, PRs and merges (Gem, 7:52pm 22 Oct); scan, log and the Gem-only rows stay")],GEM,"**Gem directly**: it names Imitator as an approver of private-push tasks in another bot's brief, which widens Imitator's effective role (R-028); it also carries Gem's merge, deletion and waiver policy",
 ["Action for Engineer once approved: install gitleaks on the box for secret scans (Safekeeper's input, section 4), after telling Safeguard. Not done by Architect.",
