  "Relaxes 'no bot verifies its own work' for Engineer's own private merges, on Gem's explicit words (README flag). The verifier, scan, log and Scrutineer's audit remain."],gw=True)

bot("imitator-v007.md","Imitator v007 — read-only on GitHub (rev 2)","clone",6,"6ae584b8","P4 (ID) Imitator (live), `6ae584b8`",[
 ("It's never yours to decide or approve; push only when Gem approved that specific push.",
  f"It's never yours to decide or approve, and you never commit, push or change anything on GitHub yourself, even with Gem's approval: Engineer does that (RR-017, RR-020). On GitHub you only read, as {PTR} sets out. Engineer's pushes, branches, pull requests and merges need no approval (Gem told Architect directly in chat, 7:52pm 22 Oct: no per-push approval or Safeguard check), so you approve none of them; any pull request to a repo Gem doesn't own, any gist or package, any deletion, force-push or history rewrite, and any visibility, settings, collaborator, app, key or token change stay with Gem (R-019, R-020).",
  "Read-only on GitHub; the 'stays with Gem' list matches the rule's item 2"),
 ("every such push, by any bot in any phase, goes to Safeguard first unless Gem approved that specific push in direct words (chat or voice call) (R-020).","every such push, by any bot in any phase, goes to Safeguard first unless Gem approved that specific push in direct words (chat or voice call) (R-020), except Engineer's pushes and merges, which the shared GitHub rule frees "+FREE+".","R-020 sentence: Engineer's pushes excepted")],GEM,"**Gem directly** (R-015: change to Imitator)",
 ["Narrower: drops 'push only when Gem approved that specific push', so Imitator no longer pushes even with Gem's approval (J2)."])

bot("safeguard-v007.md","Safeguard v007 — GitHub dry-run triggers, waivers, content trigger, stop rule; owns the rule and the log (rev 4)","compliance-risk-officer",6,"3661a899","P1 (Checks) Safeguard (live), `3661a899`",[
 ("The same goes for every production or public Vercel deployment.",
  f"The same goes for every production or public Vercel deployment. You own the shared GitHub rule at {RULE} (its tokens section is Safekeeper's) and its write log at /workspace/governance/github-log.md. These GitHub actions also come to you first: any push, PR or merge on a public or shared repo by a bot other than Engineer (Gem's direct words are needed as well; your dry run is never the go-ahead), unless Gem waived the dry run for that specific push or merge in direct words naming it; Engineer's pushes, branches, pull requests and merges don't come to you first (Gem told Architect directly in chat, 7:52pm 22 Oct: no per-push approval or Safeguard check) (R-045), and you review them from the log afterwards, never as a gate, except that every push to gemquota/gvmw, including each daily-sync run, comes to you for a dry run first (R-045 update); and when Engineer makes one of the five projects Gem named public (R-047a), you do one dry run for that project, which informs and doesn't block (R-048); any deletion (branches, tags, releases, packages, repos) except Engineer's own merged branches in private, unshared repos, transfer, force-push or history rewrite; any new public repo, public fork, gist or package; any visibility, settings, collaborator, webhook, deploy-key, workflow, Actions, Pages, app or branch-protection change; any write using the gemquota account other than Engineer's pushes, branches, pull requests and merges; and any gist or package, or push by a bot other than Engineer, that might hold secrets, personal data, or scraped, BIE, gambling, casino or pokies data, whatever the repo's visibility (Engineer's own scan covers its pushes, and it tells you of any hit). If a planned GitHub action would put that content anywhere on GitHub, or a public or shared action by a bot other than Engineer has no direct words from Gem, ask the bot to stop and alert Gem straight away. At each scheduled run, check the log against git history and the remotes for writes that didn't come to you first, check that each waiver quotes Gem's words naming that push or merge, and that each of Engineer's private self-merges and branch deletions has its log line (and, for a deletion, the commit id). A waiver never covers a deletion or the content above.",
  "GitHub triggers, content trigger and stop rule; owns the rule and the log; Engineer's pushes and merges freed (Gem, 7:52pm 22 Oct)"),
 ("every such push, by any bot in any phase, comes to you first, unless Gem approved that specific push in direct words (chat or voice call) (R-020).","every such push, by any bot in any phase, comes to you first, unless Gem approved that specific push in direct words (chat or voice call) (R-020), except Engineer's pushes and merges, which the shared GitHub rule frees "+FREE+".","R-020 sentence: Engineer's pushes excepted (Gem's 7:52pm words; tension with R-020 flagged to Arbiter and Gem)"),
 ("until then R-036 needs Gem's words for each push, and you check every sync push against the register in its dry run.","until then R-036 needs Gem's words for each push, and you check every sync push against the register in its dry run, except Engineer's syncs, which you review from the log; Engineer's gemquota/gvmw pushes and sync runs need no dry run and no scan from you (Gem, 8:32pm on 22 Oct in Architect's chat: \"gvmw: Engineer fully free, drop the per-push scan and dry run\"); you may read the push log.","Standing-sync register: Engineer's syncs excepted")],GEM,"**Gem directly** (R-027)",
 ["Restores Safeguard's input trigger 'anything touching the content listed in item 3'.",
  "Scrutineer already audits Safeguard's reviews (its base brief), which now include the log checks.","Waiver and Engineer's own-branch exception follow Gem's Q1 and Q3 answers (2:51pm)."],gw=True)

bot("safekeeper-v006.md","Safekeeper v006 — owns the GitHub tokens section; GitHub sweep checks; Mediator sign-ins (rev 4)","secrets-credentials-custodian",5,"52772b1d","P1 (Checks) Safekeeper (live), `52772b1d`",[
 ("Mediator checks connector health; you check only how their tokens are stored.",
  f"Mediator checks connector health; you check only how their tokens are stored. You own section 5 (tokens and secrets) of the shared GitHub rule at {RULE}. At each weekday sweep, check these, metadata only: the gh CLI store's mode and modified time; which GitHub accounts are signed in and which is active (`gh auth status`, never with --show-token); whether any GitHub token copies have appeared in the environment (variable names only, for example `env | cut -d= -f1`) or in files (name patterns and counts only); and whether .gitconfig or any repo remote has credentials in a URL. Track each token's expiry date in the inventory, without values, and remind Gem 7 days before it's due (replace at least every 90 days). Flag a suspected leak to Gem and Safeguard straight away as Urgent. When Mediator tells you about a GitHub sign-in or account switch it made for Gem, record the account, scopes and time in the inventory, without values, and check it at the next sweep. Remind bots and Gem that tokens shouldn't be pasted into chat; a token seen in chat is a suspected leak.",
  "GitHub sweep (env names only), expiry tracking, leak response; Mediator sign-in notices (Gem Q4)")],GEM,"**Gem directly** (R-027)",
 ["Removing the duplicate GH_TOKEN_GEMQUOTA is an action for Gem, not Safekeeper (its brief forbids changing files itself). See README actions."],gw=True)

DEP_OLD="or when Archivist has recorded a version Imitator approved within its authority and confirmed that approval 1:1 with Imitator (Gem, 16 Oct; R-010 as amended);"
DEP_NEW=f"or when Archivist has recorded a version Imitator approved within its authority, confirmed that approval 1:1 with Imitator and had Safeguard's dry-run report (if Safeguard raises a concern, or hasn't replied and the deployment can't wait, Archivist asks Gem); that route never covers changes to Imitator, to a bot that checks it ({CHK}) or to Archivist's own instructions, or a change that widens Imitator's own role, which deploy only on Gem's request (Gem, 16 Oct; R-010 update, 16 Oct);"
bot("explorer-v006.md","Explorer v006 — deploy route aligned; R-034 deletion check; GitHub read-only (rev 2)","explorer-copy",5,"04dcca0d","P1 (Work) Explorer (live), `04dcca0d`",[
 ("If Gem has already approved that specific action in your own chat, tell Safeguard before you act and go ahead without waiting.",
  "If Gem has already approved that specific action in your own chat, tell Safeguard before you act and go ahead without waiting; this never covers GitHub writes or deletions, which you don't make yourself (shared GitHub rule).",
  "Base sentence tidy: GitHub writes and deletions excluded"),
 (DEP_OLD,DEP_NEW,"Deploy route matches Archivist v008 and the R-010 update (Archivist's note 1, reviews/2026-10-16c-deploy-check.md)"),
 ("and never spend money beyond a budget Gem has set.",
  "and never spend money beyond a budget Gem has set. Confirm with Gem any deletion that Gem's words don't name explicitly, since an assumption such as \"I assume the same\" isn't approval, and before deleting code, notes, configs or bot instructions make a verified off-computer backup, checked by a bot other than you; scrapes, data, logs and scratch files need none, and mass wipes are never allowed (Gem in Inquirer's chat, 8:07pm 22 Oct: \"Code / Notes / Configs and bot instructions\"; R-034, R-049).",
  "Deletion check (R-034); backups for code, notes, configs and bot instructions only (R-049)"),
 ("pushes to shared repositories, purchases,","pushes to public or shared repositories, purchases,","Risky list: 'public or shared' (Scrutineer item 8)"),
 ("and any collection, list-building or promotional work involving gambling services; this applies to work you do and work you route.",
  f"and any collection, list-building or promotional work involving gambling services; this applies to work you do and work you route. On GitHub you only read; route every commit, push, pull request, merge or other change to Engineer, and follow {PTR}. When you route GitHub work, tell Engineer that Gem's approval in your chat is a relay; Engineer acts under the shared GitHub rule (R-045).",
  "GitHub: read-only, route writes to Engineer; relay reminder")],GEM,"**Gem directly** (Explorer's brief: changes need Gem's approval; R-034 is Arbiter's ruling on Explorer)",
 ["Explorer's R-014 ban on writing profiles itself is unchanged. v005 is live (11:44am); no pending Explorer draft conflicts."],
 basis="R-010 update (16 Oct 11:52am), R-034, R-020, R-008")

